    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We use the distributive law (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n$$(2x+3)(x+5) = 2x\\cdot x + 2x\\cdot 5 + 3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 5.$$\nNow, we simplify each term:\n$$2x\\cdot x = 2x^2,$$\n$$2x\\cdot 5 = 10x,$$\n$$3\\cdot x = 3x,$$\nand\n$$3\\cdot 5 = 15.$$\nFinally, we combine these terms by addition: \n$$2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15 = 2x^2 + 13x + 15.$$\nTherefore, the expansion of the given binomial product is \n$$\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}.$$",
